The WO₃ source comparison is decisive: the Loopstra–Boldrini monoclinic model fits substantially better than the conventional Tanisaki record, and the triclinic alternative is slightly but reproducibly worse despite extra cell freedom. The three-phase inventory is now coherent. I’m branching from the best clean checkpoint to compare neutral/size/strain/combined broadening for NiWO₄, WO₃, and NiO one phase at a time.

